{"title":"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) Find an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e87f876d93aa63957b5c8dbbf0c3e19e11dcfa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + \\ldots + n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square.\n(b) Show that there are infinitely many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> that have the property that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e87f876d93aa63957b5c8dbbf0c3e19e11dcfa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + \\ldots + n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square, and determine at least three more examples of such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\nHint: There is one approach that uses the result of a previous problem on this contest.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (Other acceptable answers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba561e4a8e69d78567a624d1bb4c2018b355a1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41, 239, 1393, 8119$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />, and, in general, anything generated by the formula in part b. The answer students are most likely to give is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II\">2018 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href